{
  "raw": {
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=921993": {
      "title": "Facility Veterinary Officer",
      "description": "Facility Veterinary Officer Faculty of Health Sciences Perth, Western Australia Permanent Part Time 31/10/2026 Part time (0.6 FTE), permanent | Curtin Bentley Campus Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide (ARWU 2025) Reference Number: 1693601 About the Role: Curtin University is seeking an experienced veterinary professional to join us as a Facility Veterinary Officer on a part-time (0.6 FTE), permanent basis. Reporting to the Technical Operations Manager, you will play an important role in ensuring animals used in research and teaching are cared for to the highest standards of veterinary care and regulatory compliance. Working across Curtin’s animal facilities, you will provide veterinary leadership and strategic advice on the use, and care of a diverse range of animals, from laboratory and aquatic species through to avian and native wildlife. The role offers considerable variety and the opportunity to use your veterinary expertise across a broad research and teaching environment. You will oversee Curtin’s veterinary care program, providing specialist advice on animal health, husbandry, welfare and biosecurity while helping to shape and promote best-practice animal care across the University. Importantly, you will work alongside researchers undertaking medical and biomedical research, providing veterinary expertise that supports their work to better understand disease and advance medical research. This is an opportunity to have a genuine influence on the ethical use and care of animals across Curtin, combining animal welfare, veterinary leadership and meaningful research impact in a unique university environment. Your responsibilities will include: Provide veterinary leadership and strategic advice on the health, care and welfare of animals used for research and teaching Oversee Curtin’s veterinary care program, ensuring compliance with the NHMRC Australian Code for the Care and Use of Animals for Scientific Purposes Lead the diagnosis and treatment of animals within Curtin’s animal facilities, including prescribing treatments and supervising restricted drug use Develop and deliver training in animal handling, procedures and care, and assess the competency of staff and researchers working with animals Provide specialist veterinary advice to Animal Facility Managers and the Technical Operations Manager on animal health, care and welfare Provide pre-AEC application consultation and veterinary advice to researchers and other animal users Who we are looking for (selection criteria): A tertiary qualification in Veterinary Science or extensive veterinary experience Eligibility for veterinary registration in Western Australia Strong interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to effectively engage with animal stakeholders and University management In-depth knowledge of legislation, standards and codes of practice governing the care and use of animals in research and teaching environments Demonstrated ability to work independently, provide specialist advice and lead and influence within your area of expertise A strong commitment to the welfare and ethical care of animals used for research and teaching Demonstrated proficiency in the responsible care and management of animals Desirable criteria: Experience working within an animal facility in a tertiary education or research environment Knowledge and/or experience in laboratory animal surgical techniques Role Requirements: As this is a continuing (permanent) role, you will require permanent work rights in Australia to be considered 22.5 hours per week. Successful candidate will have the opportunity to negotiate their preferred working schedule Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction Availability to respond to work-related matters outside standard business hours, where required Flexibility to attend animal facilities outside standard business hours, including weekends, where required About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This part time (0.6 FTE), permanent role attracts a remuneration of $122,699 - $130,758 (G08) pro rata to 0.6 FTE + 17% superannuation Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up to date resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position’s selection criteria (noted above) - no more than two pages If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Please note applications will not be accepted via this email address. Applications close: 8:00pm (AWST) on Sunday, 15 November 2026. Late applications or applications received via email will not be considered, and only successful candidates will be contacted. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. We reserve the right to remove the advert earlier than the date on the advert. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=921587": {
      "title": "Lecturer / Associate Lecturer - Korean Studies",
      "description": "Lecturer / Associate Lecturer - Korean Studies Faculty of Humanities Perth, Western Australia Contract Full Time 31/10/2026 Fixed-term Full-time 12 months from commencement date, Bentley Campus Competitive Remuneration package, 17% super & generous leave Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide Reference: 1700086 About the Role: Curtin University is seeking an Associate Lecturer (ALA) or Lecturer (ALB) in Korean Studies, specialising in Korean language, for a teaching and research position. You will contribute to the delivery, coordination and further development of the Korean Studies program, with a particular focus on online teaching, while undertaking research relevant to the your disciplinary expertise in connection to the Korea Research & Engagement Centre at Curtin University. In this role, you will play a central part in strengthening and expanding Australia’s first fully online Korean Studies major, delivered by Curtin and offered nationally through the Open Universities Australia (OUA) network. This teaching and research position also contributes to academic service and engagement. Responsibilities will reflect the appointment level: at ALA, you will develop your teaching and research profile with guidance from colleagues; at ALB, you will take on unit coordination and contribute an established research record, funding experience and research supervision capability. The balance of teaching and research will be agreed through Curtin’s Career and Performance Planning (PCP) process. Your responsibilities will include: Deliver engaging Korean language teaching from beginner to advanced levels, particularly online, developing students’ speaking, listening, reading and writing skills, assessing their work and supporting their learning. Develop and refine curriculum, learning materials and assessment to strengthen the online Korean Studies major. Contribute to unit coordination and teaching administration, with guidance appropriate to your experience and appointment level. Undertake research relevant to Korean Studies, publish scholarly outputs and contribute to the area’s major Academy of Korean Studies Core Research project and [JE1]support with further competitive funding applications. Contribute to honours and postgraduate supervision, as appropriate to your qualifications and appointment level. Participate in academic service, community engagement and a collaborative, supportive working environment. At ALA, you will develop your teaching and research profile with guidance from colleagues. At ALB, you will take greater responsibility for unit coordination, research funding applications, supervision and academic service. Who We Are Looking For: We are seeking an academic who can contribute to Korean language education, particularly online, and research relevant to Korean Studies. Applicants do not need to have their PhD in language education, but they should address the shared criteria below and the requirements for their nominated appointment level. High-level Korean language proficiency in speaking, listening, reading and writing, with demonstrated ability to teach Korean from beginner to advanced levels and a reflective approach to improving teaching and supporting student learning. Knowledge of contemporary language teaching approaches and the ability to contribute to engaging online learning materials and curriculum development. High-level communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to work collaboratively and interact with students and staff with cross-cultural sensitivity. Demonstrated commitment to applying relevant policies, procedures and legislation in teaching, research and day-to-day university activities. Associate Lecturer (ALA) Selection Criteria: Progress towards a doctoral qualification in Korean Studies or a relevant discipline. An understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to Korean language teaching. An emerging research track record or demonstrated potential to conduct quality research relevant to Korean Studies and contribute productively to the Korea Research & Engagement Centre project. Demonstrated ability to contribute to curriculum review and renewal, including Korean language learning materials. Demonstrated high-level organisational skills to manage teaching, research and associated administrative responsibilities. Lecturer (ALB) Selection Criteria: A doctoral qualification in Korean Studies or a relevant discipline. Demonstrated high-level teaching skills relevant to Korean language education and a reflective approach to teaching delivery. A strong understanding of pedagogical theory and contemporary educational practice relevant to the discipline. An established or emerging record of research outputs relevant to Korean Studies in high-quality refereed academic journals or other appropriate scholarly outlets, relative to opportunity. A history of successful competitive grant applications. Demonstrated ability to supervise higher degree research students. Demonstrated experience or capacity to undertake unit coordination, relevant to the delivery and development of Korean language units. Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This Fixed Term role attracts a remuneration of $85,872 - $115,862 (ALA) / $121,857 - $144,352 (ALB) + 17% superannuation. Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover letter outlining your interest in the role and clearly stating whether you are applying for Associate Lecturer (ALA) or Lecturer (ALB) . Demonstrate how your background meets the shared selection criteria and those specific to your nominated level, as outlined above. Please keep your letter to 2–3 pages (maximum 3 pages). If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST) Thursday 12th of November 2026. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
