    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=922003": {
      "title": "Faculty Business Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Faculty Business Operations Coordinator Faculty of Science & Engineering Perth, Western Australia Permanent Full Time 31/10/2026 Full-time, permanent position | Curtin Bentley Campus Competitive remuneration, leave, super & salary packaging provisions On-campus amenities including a gym, medical centre, and childcare facilities. Reference Number: 1700881 About the Role: We are seeking an experienced and proactive individual to join the Faculty of Science and Engineering as Faculty Business Operations Coordinator. You will coordinate operational and administrative functions for the Faculty Office, support a small team and work closely with internal service providers to deliver efficient and responsive services. This is an opportunity to make your mark, with scope to review existing ways of working, simplify processes and develop efficient, well-documented systems that support consistent service delivery. You will have the opportunity to identify improvements, take initiative and help shape how the Faculty operates. The successful candidate will bring strong planning, problem-solving and organisational skills, a process-driven approach and the ability to build effective relationships and motivate a small team to achieve positive outcomes. If you enjoy a dynamic environment and are motivated by improving processes and making a tangible difference, we encourage you to apply. Your responsibilities will include: Manage day-to-day business operations across assigned Faculty areas. Build effective relationships with university service functions and Faculty stakeholders. Develop and improve business processes to support efficient service delivery. Coordinate projects, initiatives and Faculty-wide communications. Provide executive support, including reports, briefing papers and committee support. Manage operational budgets, reporting and resource allocation. Lead and manage the administrative pool, including staffing and performance. Who we are looking for (selection criteria): Advanced interpersonal and oral communication skills with the ability to effectively consult with a wide range of stakeholders on a range of matters and in a professional and confident manner. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage multiple deliverables in a dynamic and complex environment. Developed analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to offer solutions to complex problems. Experience managing staff, with the ability to conduct effective work planning and performance review discussions and to foster a work environment of high achievement, continuous improvement, and job satisfaction. Demonstrated understanding of financial and budget management. High level written communication skills with the ability to prepare high-quality reports, briefing papers and correspondence. Desirable : Previous experience working within the higher education sector. Role Requirements: As this is a permanent position, you will require ongoing work rights in Australia. Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction Your new Team: The Faculty of Science and Engineering is committed to delivering transformative education and world-class research across a diverse range of disciplines. With strong industry partnerships and a global presence, the Faculty provides students with innovative, practice-based learning opportunities that prepare them for success in rapidly evolving fields. Our mission is to nurture talent, drive discovery, and contribute to solving real-world challenges through excellence in teaching, research, and engagement. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin 