    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=924123": {
      "title": "Business Operations Coordinator",
      "description": "Business Operations Coordinator Office of Corporate Services Perth, Western Australia Permanent Full Time 5/11/2026 Full time, permanent role l Kalgoorlie l Commencement January 2027 Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions Create a safe, connected residential experience for students! Reference : 1689574 About the Role: This is an opportunity to take a hands-on role at the heart of Curtin’s residential community in Kalgoorlie, coordinating the day-to-day business operations that help Agricola run effectively while contributing to a positive experience for residents. As Business Operations Coordinator, you will bring together operational coordination, administration, stakeholder engagement and resident support. Working closely with the Accommodation Manager, accommodation staff, University service areas and external stakeholders, you will help ensure operational matters are managed efficiently while supporting a welcoming and well-connected residential community. The role offers genuine variety. Alongside coordinating business processes, reporting, resources and administration, you will contribute to residential life programs, pastoral care and activities that encourage community living, cross-cultural connection, health, wellbeing and participation. You will also support the Accommodation Manager when complex or critical issues arise. Your responsibilities will include: Coordinate the effective day-to-day business operations of Agricola in partnership with University service areas and external stakeholders. Develop and maintain efficient administrative processes, communications, reports and correspondence. Provide clear advice on relevant policies, processes and operational matters. Coordinate residential life, social interaction and pastoral care initiatives that support community living, cross-cultural connection, health, hygiene and sporting activities. Support resource planning, budget monitoring, staffing administration and the supervision of administrative staff where required. Act as a key contact for residents and a broad range of internal and external stakeholders. Support the Accommodation Manager in responding to critical incidents, emergencies, and behavioural or disciplinary matters in line with relevant processes. Who we are looking for/Selection Criteria: You will be an organised and approachable professional who enjoys bringing people and processes together. You will be comfortable managing competing priorities, working independently when required and building trusted relationships with people from a wide variety of backgrounds. Relevant tertiary qualifications and relevant experience in residential accommodation or property management; extensive experience and broad knowledge in an administrative field; or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and education or training. Demonstrated experience coordinating, or the ability to coordinate, the operational requirements of a small business unit. Highly developed organisational skills and the ability to manage multiple deliverables in a dynamic environment. Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to build rapport and work effectively with a diverse range of internal and external stakeholders. Highly effective written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to present information clearly and professionally. The ability to work collaboratively as part of a team and independently with limited direction. Sound judgement and the ability to resolve day-to-day and critical issues appropriately. An understanding of issues relevant to young people and the capacity to provide pastoral care within a residential environment. Desirable : Previous experience in tertiary education, particularly student accommodation or working with international students, and experience mentoring young people. Role Requirements: As this is a continuing (permanent) role, you will require permanent work rights in Australia to be considered Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction Ability to work outside normal office hours when required, including participation in an on-call roster and responding to calls from residential staff on weeknights and weekends. Current Class C driver’s license. Desirable Mental Health and or First Aid Certificate. (successful applicant to complete this training once they commence) Your new Team: Accommodation, Operating Engagement Services Based at Agricola in Kalgoorlie, you will work closely with the Accommodation Manager and accommodation team, including Residential Assistants and Senior Residential Assistants. The role also works across Curtin with Student Experience services, WASM, Properties, People and Culture, Financial Services, Digital & Technology Solutions and the Curtin Safer Community Team. Your stakeholder network will extend beyond the University to current and prospective residents, families and guardians, suppliers, contractors, external organisations and emergency services where required. It is a varied role where strong relationships, sound judgement and responsive coordination make a tangible contribution to the residential community. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This Continuous G06 level role attracts a remuneration of $99,213 - $105,251 per annum + 17% superannuation . Time Well-Spent: Experience the added value of 17.5% leave loading, with the option to be paid out or taken as additional leave. Benefit from Parental Leave (26 weeks for the primary caregiver), Annual Leave (25 days), Personal Leave (14 days), Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Leave (5 days) * Travel Leave (2 days), Study Leave and Community Service Leave. Plus 18% more observed days off – enjoy 12 Public Holidays each year, including Easter Tuesday, and two extra University Days over the Christmas/New Year period. Recognition for Prior Service: Curtin recognises prior service for long service leave purposes. New Curtin employees may be* eligible if they have worked for an Australian university, public service or other recognised institution. Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position’s selection criteria (noted above) - no more than two pages , OR A document addressing the selection criteria for the role If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST), Sunday 22nd of November 2026. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=923242": {
      "title": "Business Manager - Research & Finance",
      "description": "Business Manager - Research & Finance Faculty of Business & Law Perth, Western Australia Contract Full Time 4/11/2026 Fixed-term Full-Time Ending 9th December 2029, Perth City Campus Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide (ARWU 2025) Reference: 1699932 About the Role: As Business Manager, Research and Finance, you will lead financial management and research operations for the Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age (QWiDA). Led by Curtin University, this nationally significant research centre operates across eight participating universities, known as nodes. You will help keep the Centre well managed, meet its complex budget, reporting and contractual requirements, and demonstrate progress against its objectives. Reporting to the Chief Operating Officer (COO), you will be the key link between the Centre, Curtin’s service areas and the participating universities on finance and research administration. You will provide expert advice, oversee budget development and monitoring, and help ensure the Centre meets its obligations under the ARC Funding Agreement and partner agreements. As a foundational appointment in the Centre’s first year, this role offers a unique opportunity to design the financial and research administration framework of a multi-institution Centre from the ground up. Your responsibilities will include: Develop and monitor the Centre’s annual budget, forecasts and research project budgets, in consultation with the Chief Operating Officer, Director and the University’s finance. Lead regular budget reviews and re-forecasts with the Director, COO and Centre leads, reporting on expenditure, variances and risks and recommending corrective action. Design, implement and continuously improve the Centre’s finance and research administration systems and processes that ensure compliance while supporting and enabling researchers to manage their finances effectively, without adding unnecessary layers of bureaucracy, and assure the quality of transactional finance processing undertaken by Centre staf Lead the Centre’s financial reporting and acquittals to the ARC, Curtin and partner organisations, including node cash and in-kind contribution reporting. Manage all reporting and contractual obligations of the Centre, including the ARC Funding Agreement and partner and multi-institutional agreements. Provide expert advice to the COO, the Director, researchers and Centre leads on operational and regulatory matters pertaining to research, the University’s research and financial processes, and the research project lifecycle, from proposal and budget development through to project closure. Oversee Centre cost centres and node-level financial arrangements, ensuring compliance with ARC, University and partner financial requirements and reporting standards. Oversee the administration of internal funding schemes, including budgets, application and approval processes, payments and acquittals. Develop, document and maintain the Centre’s finance and research administration policies, procedures and guidelines, consistent with University and ARC requirements, and provide clear advice to staff and nodes on their application. Work with node administrators to ensure node financial and KPI data is accurate, timely and consistent across all nodes. Liaise and collaborate with University service groups, including Finance, the Research Office, Human Resources and Properties, and with the ARC and external partners. Other duties as directed, consistent with the classification level of the role. Who we are looking for: To be successful in this role, you will have previous experience in a leadership and management role, with highly developed financial management, reporting and monitoring skills. You will have demonstrated experience managing research funding, including project budgets, reporting and acquittals, and the ability to interpret financial information and make clear recommendations to senior leaders. You will have very good knowledge of research finance and funding administration, gained through relevant experience, training or qualifications. You will build strong relationships and negotiate effectively with a wide range of internal and external stakeholders, including across multiple institutions. A formal qualification is not essential, but the following will be highly regarded: Experience within an ARC Centre of Excellence or a similar multi-institution research or higher education environment Completion of a relevant postgraduate qualification, or membership of, or progress towards membership of, an internationally recognised accounting body Your New Team - ARC Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age: Despite growing investment in digital transformation, the potential of technology to improve the quality of work has not been fully realised. The Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age (QWiDA) aims to address this challenge by bringing together leading researchers alongside industry and government partners from institutions across Australia and the globe to explore how new technologies can be integrated responsibly to create and sustain productive, inclusive and healthy work. The Centre brings together diverse experts from social and technical disciplines across three interlinked research streams: Augmented Working, Networked Workplaces and Future-Ready Workforce. To learn more about QWiDA, please visit qwida.org.au Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role. Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This Fixed Term G08 level role attracts a remuneration of $122,699 - $130,758 + 17% superannuation. Based on our Perth city campus Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position selection criteria – 2 – 3 Pages Max If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST) Thursday 26th of November 2026. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=923167": {
      "title": "Administrative Officer - Quality Work in Digital Age",
      "description": "Administrative Officer - Quality Work in Digital Age Faculty of Business & Law Perth, Western Australia Contract Full Time 4/11/2026 Fixed-term Full-Time Ending 9th December 2029, Perth City Campus Generous Leave Entitlements + 17% super contributions Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide (ARWU 2025) Reference: 1699985 About the Role: The Administrative Officer provides day-to-day administrative support to ensure all services are provided efficiently to meet the operating needs of the Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age (QWiDA). The role has particular responsibility for the day-to-day maintenance of QWiDA’s central operational database(s), which the Centre relies on to record, track and report on its activities across eight university nodes. As a member of the QWiDA Operations Team, the Administrative Officer will work closely with node administrators and professional staff across Curtin and the Centre’s university nodes, helping to maintain consistent record-keeping and administrative practice across the Centre’s national network. You will be the main point of contact for node administrators on the collection of KPI and financial data, so accuracy, follow-through and attention to detail are essential. As a foundational appointment in the Centre’s first year, this role offers the chance to help shape how data is collected and reported across a multi-institution network. Your responsibilities will include: Act as the main point of contact for node administrators for the collection of KPI and financial data, coordinating timelines, following up outstanding returns and maintaining a clear record of what has been received. Maintain the accuracy, completeness and currency of records held in QWiDA’s central database, including data entry, data cleansing and routine quality checks. Escalate complex data discrepancies as required and maintain up-to-date key performance indicator (KPI) records to support Centre, Executive and ARC reporting requirements. Work collaboratively with administrative staff across QWiDA’s university nodes to share information, follow consistent administrative practice and facilitate administrative efficiency. Provide financial administration support, including raising purchase orders, processing invoices, reconciling credit card expenditure and processing reimbursements in line with university procedures and financial delegations. Support the administration of internal funding schemes, including collating applications, tracking progress and processing payments. Support the administration of recruitment, onboarding and induction processes for Centre staff, students and postdoctoral researchers, including the maintenance of associated records. Support Centre events, workshops, meetings and visitors, including venue and catering bookings, event advertising, registrations, visitor arrangements, on-the-day logistics and post-event attendee reporting, and assist with website updates and event promotion. Other duties as directed, consistent with the classification level of the role. Who we are looking for: To be successful in this role, you will have previous experience maintaining data within databases or similar business systems, with a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. You will have a demonstrated ability to collate information from multiple people or organisations and follow up to meet reporting deadlines, along with sound financial administration practices and well-developed communication skills for working with diverse groups across different institutions. You will hold a relevant certificate or diploma-level qualification, or have an equivalent combination of relevant experience and training. Experience in the following areas will be highly regarded: Experience working in a university, research institute or multi-institutional research centre environment Experience using a low-code database or CRM platform Experience supporting research student or research administration processes Demonstrated experience in event planning, management and delivery Your New Team - ARC Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age: Despite growing investment in digital transformation, the potential of technology to improve the quality of work has not been fully realised. The Australian Research Council (ARC) Centre of Excellence for Quality Work in a Digital Age (QWiDA) aims to address this challenge by bringing together leading researchers alongside industry and government partners from institutions across Australia and the globe to explore how new technologies can be integrated responsibly to create and sustain productive, inclusive and healthy work. The Centre brings together diverse experts from social and technical disciplines across three interlinked research streams: Augmented Working, Networked Workplaces and Future-Ready Workforce. To learn more about QWiDA, please visit qwida.org.au Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role. Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This Fixed Term G05 level role attracts a remuneration of $85,781 - $93,836 + 17% superannuation. Based on our Perth city campus Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position – 2 – 3 Pages Max If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST) Sunday 15th of November 2026. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=923099": {
      "title": "Research Associate",
      "description": "Research Associate Faculty of Science & Engineering Perth, Western Australia Contract Full Time 4/11/2026 Two-year fixed term, full-time opportunity | Possibility of 1-year extension Contribute to an innovative ARC-funded Discovery Project with environmental and Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide (ARWU 2026) Job Reference: 1700867 Are you a researcher with expertise in microbiology, biogeochemistry, geomicrobiology or mineral–microbe interactions? Join an innovative research project investigating how microbial processes can transform chrysotile and other magnesium-rich silicate asbestos minerals into more stable, less hazardous forms. About the Role: The Research Associate will contribute to the Australian Research Council (ARC) Discovery Project Microbial Detoxification of Chrysotile , led by Dr Navdeep K. Dhami, Senior Lecturer at Curtin University. Bringing together microbiology, geochemistry and mineral science, the project investigates how microbial communities, biofilms and microbial metabolic pathways influence the transformation of chrysotile and other magnesium-rich silicate asbestos minerals into more stable, less hazardous forms. Working with the project lead and research collaborators, you will design and conduct experiments to investigate the biochemical, microbiological and molecular mechanisms underpinning microbial asbestos degradation, including mineral dissolution, elemental cycling and the formation of secondary mineral phases. Your research will advance fundamental understanding of microbial mineral weathering and biomineralisation while exploring the potential of magnesium-rich transformation products for carbon dioxide (CO₂) capture and mineral carbonation. This interdisciplinary opportunity sits at the intersection of mineral transformation, environmental remediation and climate research, with the potential to contribute to safer asbestos management and remediation and broader net-zero emissions objectives. Your responsibilities will include: Designing and conducting experiments to investigate microbial weathering mechanisms and reaction kinetics at the molecular level. Investigating microbe–mineral interactions and the biochemical, microbiological and molecular processes associated with asbestos mineral transformation. Characterising mineral transformation pathways and contributing to research on biomineralisation and mineral carbonation. Publishing research outcomes in high-quality, peer-reviewed journals and other appropriate research outlets. Disseminating research findings through academic seminars, workshops and conferences. Providing effective supervision to Honours, research Master’s and doctoral students. Contributing to competitive research funding applications as a co-investigator or chief investigator, as appropriate. Developing and maintaining collaborative relationships with researchers, professional bodies, industry, government departments and the wider community. Contributing to a collegial, supportive and inclusive research environment, as well as relevant academic service, leadership and administrative activities. Participating in appropriate professional development and mentoring opportunities. Who We Are Looking For (Selection Criteria): You are a capable and collaborative researcher with a strong foundation in relevant scientific disciplines and a demonstrated commitment to high-quality research. You can plan and conduct experimental investigations, communicate research findings effectively and contribute to multidisciplinary research teams. To be successful in this role, you will also satisfy the following Essential Criteria: A PhD (or with no more than ~6 months until completion at the time of interview) in Microbiology, Biogeochemistry, Geology, Civil Engineering or a related discipline. Experience in microbial culturing and molecular identification techniques. Experience with microscopic, elemental and mineralogical characterisation techniques. A strong record of research outputs in high-quality, Q1-ranked peer-reviewed journals or equivalent discipline-appropriate research outlets. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. The ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a multidisciplinary team. Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role. Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction. Interstate and/or overseas travel may be required. Work outside normal office hours may occasionally be necessary. Your new Team: You’ll join the School of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, working with Dr Navdeep K. Dhami and a collaborative team of researchers across environmental biogeotechnology, microbiology, geochemistry and mineral science. Led by Dr Dhami, the ARC Discovery Project brings together expertise in microbial–mineral interactions, biomineralisation and geochemical processes to investigate innovative approaches to asbestos detoxification and safer disposal. The project also involves research collaborators Professor Allan Pring and Professor Carlos Rodriguez-Navarro, bringing complementary expertise in mineral science and mineral transformation. You’ll be part of an interdisciplinary research environment tackling an important environmental challenge, advancing fundamental scientific knowledge while exploring opportunities for safer asbestos management and carbon capture. To learn more about the school, please visit https://www.curtin.edu.au/about/learning-teaching/science-engineering/school-of-civil-mechanical-engineering/. Our commitment to a diverse and inclusive workplace: At Curtin University, we are passionate about fostering an inclusive, diverse and welcoming environment in which all people feel respected, valued and safe. Curtin is dedicated to promoting gender equity and inclusivity in all areas. We are proud of our achievements to date and recognise that there is more to do to improve employment outcomes for women and people of diverse gender identities, particularly in STEMM disciplines. As an Athena SWAN accredited institution, we celebrate diversity and actively work to advance the representation of women and gender-diverse people in STEMM areas and empower individuals so they can thrive in their careers through a range of supportive initiatives, including leadership training, mentorship for early career progression and promotion, networking opportunities, and other professional development resources. As reflected in the Athena Swan Charter, gender equality is a broader issue that extends beyond barriers affecting women alone, and we are committed to addressing these challenges holistically. Additionally, we offer staff a competitive remuneration and benefits package, including but not limited to: 17% superannuation, plus a variety of salary packaging options. Paid Parental leave (26 weeks for the primary caregiver and 3 weeks for non-primary) subject to eligibility criteria outlined in the Enterprise Agreement; personal leave (14 days) and annual leave (20 days) Enjoy 12 Public Holidays each year (including Easter Tuesday!), and 2 extra University Days over the Christmas/New Year Period (see EBA 51.1 and 51.9). Breastfeeding facilities and campus-based childcare (where priority of placement is given to Curtin staff and students) Flexible work arrangements including return to work provisions On-campus medical centre Academic Carer Support Scheme and other diversity, inclusion and belonging initiatives detailed via the below link. We believe that diverse perspectives fuel innovation and drive excellence, and we encourage women, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander peoples, people of diverse gender, sex and sexuality, people with disability and people from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds to join us in shaping the future of STEMM together and making tomorrow better. To find out more about our comprehensive diversity, inclusion and belonging initiatives, please visit https://www.curtin.edu.au/about/values-vision-strategy/diversity-equity/gender-equity-and-inclusion/ About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2026 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This two-year fixed term, full-time ALA level role attracts a remuneration of $104,165 - $115 ,862 (ALA.5 – ALA.8) + 17% superannuation . Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and a variety food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and experience A document addressing the selection criteria for the role (noted above) If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST), Wednesday, 11 November 2026 Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=922793": {
      "title": "Accreditation & Quality Manager (S51)",
      "description": "Accreditation & Quality Manager (S51) Faculty of Business & Law Perth, Western Australia Permanent Full Time 3/11/2026 Ongoing role, Full-time, Bentley Campus Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide Reference: 1679809 At Curtin we are committed to embedding the voices and perspectives of Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander peoples at the forefront of our decision-making to create an environment in which everyone thrives. In line with Curtin’s 2030 Strategic Plan, Curtin University is committed to optimising employment outcomes for Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. In an effort to increase Aboriginal and Torres Strait representation in the University, Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are strongly encouraged to apply for this role, pursuant to Section 51 of the Equal Opportunity Act 1984 (WA). About the Role: As the Accreditation and Quality Assurance Manager, you will lead accreditation and rankings activities for the Faculty of Business and Law (FBL), while contributing to academic quality assurance outcomes in collaboration with relevant stakeholders. You will help ensure the Faculty’s courses meet University, regulatory and accreditation standards and deliver consistent academic quality across Perth, global campuses and international education partners. Working closely with senior Faculty leaders, you will contribute to the implementation of Curtin’s Quality Assurance Framework, manage accreditation reporting and reviews, and use data to guide improvements and rankings strategies. You will also lead staff and provide expert advice to help schools and partners understand and meet their accreditation and quality obligations. You will be supported by an approachable and collaborative leadership team, providing guidance and support to help you succeed in the role. Your responsibilities will include: Lead accreditation: Manage the Faculty’s accreditation portfolio, including annual and periodic reporting, major submissions, peer reviews and relationships with accreditation bodies AACSB and EFMD. Oversee academic quality: Implement Curtin’s Quality Assurance Framework, coordinate course evaluation and reporting, and support compliance with accreditation standards, TEQSA requirements, the ESOS Act and University policies. Support consistent international delivery: Work with Faculty leaders, global campuses and education partners to monitor international program outcomes and maintain standards comparable with Perth-based courses. Review staff qualification requirements: Oversee reviews of onshore and offshore academic appointments against TEQSA and AACSB faculty qualification requirements. Drive planning and improvement: Identify and scope accreditation, quality assurance and rankings projects; develop business cases and implementation plans; and coordinate delivery with stakeholders. Manage rankings activities: Lead course and business school rankings strategies, coordinate data and reputation contacts, assure submission quality, and analyse and report results. Provide expert advice and reporting: Advise senior leaders, schools and partners on accreditation and quality requirements, ensure reporting data is accurate, and report outcomes to Faculty leadership and the Advisory Council. Lead people and collaboration: Manage recruitment, induction, work priorities and staff development; collaborate across University teams; and represent the Deans of Learning and Teaching and International on relevant committees as required. Who we are looking for: You will bring a collaborative approach, sound judgement and the ability to turn complex requirements into clear advice and practical improvements. You will be confident managing competing priorities and building effective relationships with senior leaders, academic teams and international partners. Demonstrated knowledge of the Australian higher education system and the current issues affecting the sector, along with knowledge of business school accreditation standards and quality assurance frameworks, will be highly regarded. Role Requirements: As this is a continuing (permanent) role, you will require permanent work rights in Australia to be considered Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction Interstate and overseas travel may be required, along with the ability to work outside normal office hours when required. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This Continuous G09 level role attracts a remuneration of $142,841 - $150,891 + 17% superannuation. Flexible working arrangements can be discussed at interview, taking into account your needs and the requirements of the role. Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up-to-date Resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position. 2 – 3 Pages Max If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Applications will not be accepted via this email address, and late applications will not be accepted. Applications close: 8pm (AWST) Tuesday 17th of November 2026. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, remove the advert, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. Back to search results"
    },
    "https://staff.curtin.edu.au/job-vacancies/?ja-job=922366": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer - Dietetics",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer - Dietetics Faculty of Health Sciences Perth, Western Australia Contract Part Time 2/11/2026 Part time (0.6 FTE), fixed term until 31 December 2029 | Curtin Bentley Campus Ranked in the top 1% of universities worldwide Competitive remuneration + 17% super contributions | Commencing from Jan 2027 Reference Number: 1704113 About the Role: Join Curtin’s School of Population Health as a Lecturer (ALB) or Senior Lecturer (ALC) within the Master of Dietetics Program. This part-time (0.6 FTE), fixed-term (until 31 Dec 2029) teaching and research position offers an exciting opportunity to help prepare highly capable, career-ready dietetics graduates in a vibrant and collegial academic environment. We are looking for a dietitian with contemporary professional expertise and experience in areas such as individual case management, clinical reasoning, medical nutrition therapy and supporting people with complex or multiple nutrition-related conditions. You will bring this experience into the classroom, contributing to high-quality teaching, curriculum development, assessment and student support. You will also contribute to research and scholarship aligned with your expertise and career stage, while using your industry experience and professional networks to strengthen placement-based learning and connections with contemporary practice. We particularly welcome applicants who can bring fresh perspectives or expertise in emerging areas of dietetic practice. Your responsibilities will include: Teaching Provide strategic leadership and contribute to ongoing curriculum evolution of the Master of Dietetics program. Contribute to the ongoing development and delivery of the Master of Dietetics curriculum, with a particular focus on individual case management, medical nutrition therapy and professional practice learning. Design and deliver high‑quality and innovative practice informed learning experiences for postgraduate student dietitians, including tutorials, seminars, simulation and placement supervision. Contribute to unit coordination, assessment and constructive feedback that support student development and graduate readiness Apply reflective, inclusive, culturally responsive and evidence-informed approaches to teaching and student support Contribute to supervision and assessment of student dietitians during professional practice placements Research Develop research and/or scholarship of learning and teaching appropriate to your expertise and appointment level. Contribute to research through peer‑reviewed publications, seminars, and national and international conferences. Supervise postgraduate research students and support their academic development. Build collaborations with colleagues, health services, communities and industry, working toward national recognition in your field and managing associated administrative requirements. Engagement Build productive relationships with industry and external stakeholders to enhance teaching, research, and placement opportunities. Contribute to advancing the dietetics profession through active involvement in Dietitians Australia. Foster a positive, inclusive, and collegial workplace culture, contributing to School- and University‑wide activities. Who we are looking for (selection criteria): Current Accredited Practising Dietitian recognised by Dietitians Australia with a completed doctorate, progress towards a doctorate, or qualifications and substantial professional experience assessed as providing appropriate academic equivalence. Contemporary dietetic practice experience relevant to individual case management and medical nutrition therapy, including assessment, clinical reasoning, intervention planning, monitoring and evaluation Experience designing or contributing to high-quality learning experiences and communicate complex ideas to diverse learners and a reflective approach to teaching delivery. Experience with applying Dietitians Australia National Competency Standards, Accreditation Standards for Dietetics Education Programs and experience in assessing competency development of student dietitians Evidence of quality improvement, research or scholarship of learning and teaching outputs. Excellent communication and relationship building skills with a commitment to fostering a collegial environment and interacting with students and staff with cross-cultural sensitivity. Commitment to applying relevant policies and procedures in daily responsibilities. Level C (in addition to the above) A doctoral qualification in dietetics or relevant discipline. Experience providing leadership in curriculum development, academic quality and strategic development of individual case management and related areas of the Master of Dietetics program. Ability to lead curriculum development, mentor colleagues and contribute to strategic program development. Evidence of research outputs in high-quality academic journals, a history of successful competitive grant applications, and evidence of a growing national and/or international profile. Desirable Advanced or emerging practice expertise in an area that would broaden the capabilities of the dietetics team. Experience in complex chronic disease, disability, aged care, rehabilitation, mental health, paediatrics, private practice or multidisciplinary care. If you do not hold a PhD qualification, please outline your equivalent experience in your cover letter with reference to the following document: https://tinyurl.com/3r6yfaz4 Please note that if your qualifications or experience look different from what we've described above, but you feel your skills and potential are a match to the capabilities we need, please apply. We are looking for diversity in experience. Role Requirements: As this is a fixed-term contract, you will require current work rights in Australia that match the tenure of this role Successful applicants are subject to a National Police Clearance, and background, integrity, and reference checks to Curtin’s satisfaction Your New Team: School of Population Health The School of Population Health is dedicated to improving health and wellbeing outcomes for communities both locally and globally. Bringing together expertise across public health, psychology and interdisciplinary health fields, the School is recognised for its collaborative culture, innovative teaching and impactful research. Home to a dynamic community of academics, researchers and industry-connected professionals, the School is committed to addressing some of today’s most significant health challenges - from mental health and emerging diseases to climate change, population growth and health equity. Through its strong focus on education, research and community engagement, the School continues to shape the next generation of health professionals and create meaningful impact across the health sector. About Curtin University Curtin University proudly stands among the top one percent of global universities according to the ARWU 2025 rankings. We are an energetic, dedicated team of academics and professionals working together to provide global solutions through quality graduates and innovative research. Curtin is a welcoming space where integrity, respect for one another, courage, excellence, and impact are essential to everyday life. First Nations people, those identifying as LGBTQIA+, parents, carers, people of all ages, abilities and genders, and people of diverse ethnicity, nationality and faith are encouraged to apply. Our aim is to create a workforce that reflects the diversity of the community in which we live. For more information, please visit our Diversity and Inclusion page - https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/diversity-equity-and-inclusion-at-curtin/ What We Offer You: This part time (0.6 FTE), fixed-term (until 31 Dec 2029) role attracts a remuneration of $121,857 - $144,352 (ALB) / $148,847 - $171,344 (ALC) pro rata to 0.6 FTE + 17% superannuation *Please note that each candidate will be assessed based on their skills, qualifications, and experience to determine the salary level and contract duration. Situated on Whadjuk Nyungar Country, our vibrant Bentley campus includes an art gallery, gym, childcare and medical centre, bus station, accessible parking and endless food options including a supermarket. Aside from the vibrant campus life, we offer more than just a job. Curtin offers a wide range of generous benefits, including additional leave, salary packaging, health and wellbeing services and an array of discounts for retail, travel and much more. For more reasons to work at Curtin, please visit https://staff.curtin.edu.au/discover-curtin/ Join Us! If this sounds like your next role, please click APPLY NOW ensuring to attach the following documents: Up to date resume Cover Letter outlining your interest and demonstrating how your background meets the position’s selection criteria (noted above) - no more than four pages o Please confirm what level role you are applying for (ALB Lecturer or ALC Senior Lecturer) If you have any queries in relation to this opportunity or the application process, please contact our careers team on CurtinCareers@curtin.edu.au or 08 9266 9000 (option 3,1), quoting the reference number. Please note applications will not be accepted via this email address. Applications close: 8:00pm (AWST) on Sunday, 22 November 2026. Late applications or applications received via email will not be considered, and only successful candidates will be contacted. Please note we are not accepting applications from recruitment agencies at this time. Curtin reserves the right at its sole discretion to withdraw from the recruitment process, not to make an appointment, or to appoint by invitation, at any time. We reserve the right to remove the advert earlier than the date on the advert. Back to search results"
